Make pane-adoption failures diagnosable, add end-to-end test

The adoption feature (`O` key to take over foreign tmux panes) has several
silent failure paths that make "I pressed O and nothing happened" indistinguishable
from "it's working correctly and there's genuinely nothing to adopt":

1. No adoptable tools configured → scan bails with no UI signal.
2. Scan runs, finds zero candidates → no UI feedback short of reading logs.
3. Rejected candidates (one signal only, not confident) → silent drop.
4. `adopt_sockets` config option is undocumented, so panes on non-default
   tmux sockets are invisible with no hint why.

Fixes:

- Enrich adoptedMsg to carry diagnostic data (candidates seen, rejected summary).
- Store the last scan result on the Model; use it to build a diagnostic message
  in takeOverAdopted() explaining WHY no candidates are available instead of
  a generic message regardless of cause.
- Document adopt_sockets in configuration.md top-level options.
- Add a note in usage.md adoption section about socket scanning.
- Add TestAdoptionE2E: full end-to-end test chain (real foreign pane → scan
  discovers it → board shows it → O key → confirm → taken over). This closes
  a regression gap where individual stages are tested in isolation but the
  wiring between them was not, which is exactly the kind of breakage that would
  produce "O doesn't work" silently.

Messages now distinguish:
- "no agents found (run a scan, or check if agents are on a different
  tmux socket; see docs/configuration.md for adopt_sockets)" → no candidates
- "no adopted panes to take over: 3 found but rejected — not confident=3" →
  candidates were rejected due to missing signals
- The original generic message only when all candidates are actually adopted.

